---
name: walk_minutes
description: >
  What a walk costs, appended to a live decide observation (issue #826).
  Rendered by cognition.walk_minutes_line() and folded into
  observe_and_decide's observation when the step loop threads a SimClock and
  the world has a map. Penn legs are long -- Van Pelt to Houston Hall is ~57
  sim-minutes -- but the exits list prices every destination identically, so an
  agent forms "quick coffee run" intentions that are two-hour round trips.
  planner.median_travel_minutes gives the PLANNER a travel budget; this is the
  per-tick decide's equivalent. The estimate is a per-destination BFS distance
  field over the collision grid (WorldMap.walk_steps_from, #866) -- it walks
  around walls, so the price matches the leg the agent will actually take.
  Still "at least about": the BFS lands at the nearest destination tile and
  the patched walk_path routes a few tiles further, so it is a tight lower
  bound. The destination list is
  assembled in Python (it is data), like nearby_affordances; only the wording
  lives here. The deterministic mock reads only the observation's first line, so
  this can never change a mock decision.
inputs:
  destinations:
    type: string
    description: >
      Pre-joined "<name> <minutes> min" fragments, nearest first, e.g.
      "Van Pelt — Moelis Reading Room 0 min; Houston Hall 27 min".
sample:
  destinations: "Van Pelt — Moelis Reading Room 0 min; Houston Hall 27 min"
---
Walking from here takes at least about: {{ destinations }}.
